course: dictionary
lesson: 1603
title: Cheer: a shout or a feeling
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word cheer can mean a loud shout, a feeling of happiness, or a phrase that makes someone happier. Context tells you which meaning is right. Look for clues such as a crowd, a party, a friend or a team.
explain: «At last, right above their heads, they hear cheering, stamping and glasses clinking.» Crowds, stamping and glasses show a noisy party, so cheering means loud shouts of happiness.
explain: «They cheered, and he felt better than after all the excuses.» Here cheering helped someone feel happier, so cheer is about lifting spirits, like cheer up.
explain: «Ah, they're braw, cheers, wee yin.» Morven is in Edinburgh, and she is thanking Iona, so cheers means thanks here. Always check your meaning by putting it back into the sentence.
fact: To cheer is to shout loudly to show you are pleased or to encourage someone.
fact: A cheer is a shout of happiness, praise or support.
fact: To cheer someone up is to make them feel happier; to cheer up is to start feeling happier.
fact: «Cheers!» can be said when drinking, and in the UK, Ireland and Australia it can also mean thanks or goodbye.
fact: Cheer without a or s, as in «Christmas cheer», means happiness and good spirits.
exercise: At the sports day, the crowd began to cheer for the runners. What does cheer mean here? | *To shout loudly to encourage them | To go quietly home | To cook a meal | To fall asleep
exercise: Morven says «cheers» when Iona lends her the clips. What does cheers mean here? | A glass raised in a toast only | *Thanks | Goodbye forever | A loud crowd
exercise: Iona's kind drawing helped her sad friend. Which phrase means to make someone feel happier? | *cheer up | cheer for | three cheers | cheer on
test: «The crowd cheered when the goal went in.» What does cheered show? | Silence | *Pleasure and support | Sleep | Anger
test: What does cheer mean in «Christmas cheer»? | *Happiness and good spirits | A loud shout | A small gift | Sadness
exam: Which meaning of cheered is right in «They cheered, and he felt better than after all the excuses»? | Gave him a detention | *Made him feel happier | Made him argue | Ran away from him
